The comment `@@@ The last element in the list equals the appended element after add.` specifies that after the `add` operation, the element at the last index of the list (i.e., at index `size() - 1`) should be equal to the element `e` that was appended.

We can express this using the `get` method to access the last element, and compare it with `e`. Since the size increases by one after the addition, the last index is `\result ?` — but note: the method returns `true`, so `\result` is `true`, which is not useful here.

Instead, we rely on `this.size()` after the call, and access `this.get(this.size() - 1)`.

Thus, the assertion is that the last element (`get(size() - 1)`) equals `e`.

<code>assert this.get(this.size() - 1).equals(e);</code>
